      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved** — All checks pass. [[trajectory](http://go/tj/7e7a659e-bb42-4b1e-a333-361bc1d660eb)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** `Size: S (+11, -3)`. This is a small, atomic CL making a single, focused logical change.\n*   **Functionality:** ✅ The device tree changes correctly double the AHB clock frequency while adjusting the APB divider to maintain its original frequency, and correctly update the SPI reference frequency to match.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ The configuration correctly overrides the appropriate `soc.dtsi` for the ET171 FPMCU.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** ✅ Device tree configuration is direct and minimal.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Standard and idiomatic Zephyr Device Tree syntax.\n*   **Testing:** ✅ Hardware/Physical Exception applies. The CL correctly relies on manual hardware testing on `srebrna` and `sanok` to verify the CPU frequency increase and its effect on enrollment/matching time, which is appropriate for low-level CPU clock adjustments.\n*   **Security:** ✅ No security concerns with this configuration change.\n*   **Commit Message:** ✅ The commit message is well-written—it provides a clear high-level summary of the change, details the rationale (speeding up enrollment), documents the power consumption trade-offs, and correctly specifies the manual testing performed.",
